<body>
    <h1>Partner Pricing V2: Business Requirements</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <div class=3D"contentLayout2">
<style>[data-colorid=3Dll6s7ko8z2]{color:#77ecc2} html[data-color-mode=3Dda=
rk] [data-colorid=3Dll6s7ko8z2]{color:#13885e}</style>
<div class=3D"columnLayout fixed-width" data-layout=3D"fixed-width">
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell">
<div class=3D"panel" style=3D"background-color: #006A56;border-width: 1px;"=
>
<div class=3D"panelContent" style=3D"background-color: #006A56;">
<p local-id=3D"9c2e9f0b69c6"><span class=3D"legacy-color-text-inverse">Summ=
ary of Salesforce configuration and runtime changes needed to support Partn=
er Pricing V2, including pricing-model fields, context updates, data setup,=
 and cutover steps.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"bd8adfd5234a"><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lo=
zenge-visual-refresh aui-lozenge-complete">BUSINESS REQUIREMENTS</span> <sp=
an class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-visual-refresh">LAST MODIF=
IED: 04/24/2026</span></p>
<h2 local-id=3D"ad4b023a96b6" id=3D"PartnerPricingV2:BusinessRequirements-S=
ummary">Summary</h2>
<p local-id=3D"31f5a0f79b36">Partner Pricing V2 introduces two changes to t=
he existing partner pricing design.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"columnLayout two-equal" data-layout=3D"two-equal">
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell">
<div class=3D"panel" style=3D"background-color: #11719C;border-width: 1px;"=
>
<div class=3D"panelContent" style=3D"background-color: #11719C;">
<h3 local-id=3D"717636428fc8" id=3D"PartnerPricingV2:BusinessRequirements-L=
ine-LevelModelSelection"><span class=3D"legacy-color-text-inverse">Line-Lev=
el Model Selection</span></h3>
<p local-id=3D"0c6305477dbc"><span class=3D"legacy-color-text-inverse">The =
quote still selects the overall partner pricing model family. V2 then choos=
es the exact partner pricing model record for each quote line by using the =
line's product hierarchy.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell">
<div class=3D"panel" style=3D"background-color: #11719C;border-width: 1px;"=
>
<div class=3D"panelContent" style=3D"background-color: #11719C;">
<h3 local-id=3D"b189676628b3" id=3D"PartnerPricingV2:BusinessRequirements-D=
eal-Type-SpecificDiscounts"><span class=3D"legacy-color-text-inverse">Deal-=
Type-Specific Discounts</span></h3>
<p local-id=3D"b4be6ac2b70a"><span class=3D"legacy-color-text-inverse">When=
 the quote deal type is </span><em><strong><span data-colorid=3D"ll6s7ko8z2=
">Fortra Originated</span></strong></em><span class=3D"legacy-color-text-in=
verse">, V2 uses a separate Non-Originating percentage field set. All other=
 deal types continue to use the standard percentage fields.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"columnLayout fixed-width" data-layout=3D"fixed-width">
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell">
<h2 local-id=3D"636e92ffe59d" id=3D"PartnerPricingV2:BusinessRequirements-O=
bjectChanges">Object Changes</h2>
<div class=3D"panel" style=3D"background-color: #E3E3E3;border-width: 1px;"=
>
<div class=3D"panelContent" style=3D"background-color: #E3E3E3;">
<p local-id=3D"d06f1dfec017">The <code>Partner_Pricing_Model__c</code> obje=
ct must support hierarchy-based model selection and the additional discount=
 field set used for Fortra-originated deals.</p>
</div>
</div>
<h3 local-id=3D"e3a2be6f64c4" id=3D"PartnerPricingV2:BusinessRequirements-P=
artnerPricingModelFields">Partner Pricing Model Fields</h3>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"1800" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"9=
314fc3d916e" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"45af2eba2ca0">
<th data-local-id=3D"9eb4dcd83247" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"715ccb9960f7">Field Group</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"25ae5658e9b8" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"dae74c7f5a18">Fields</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"6c42c2de9561" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"0e1d4775fc13">How They Are Used</p></th>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"3ad814f325c6">
<td data-local-id=3D"6f6e04393e5b" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"7412731f2354"><strong>Hierarchy fields</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"f0037cc5a835" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"6042e4d3b508"><code>Unit__c</code></p>
<p local-id=3D"54db4b628a34"><code>Solution_Group__c</code></p>
<p local-id=3D"4c2b2cfc3db5"><code>Solution_Category__c</code></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"16a82190fed2" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"6aee20df21f8">These fields allow one partner pricing model r=
ecord to apply at a specific product hierarchy level.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b687105a04a7">They are intended to represent one hierarchy l=
evel per record, not a combined three-field key.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"40ffbc7ab79e">
<td data-local-id=3D"b3a42a3f9046" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"36acd4a60d98"><strong>Non-Originating discount fields</stron=
g></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"27f9b73d2c43" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"d2b9656ff72f"><code>Non_Orig_Software_Pct__c</code></p>
<p local-id=3D"bdc4be4d34d2"><code>Non_Orig_Subscription_Pct__c</code></p>
<p local-id=3D"84f1ff6da28d"><code>Non_Orig_New_Maint_Pct__c</code></p>
<p local-id=3D"7c8afb65e864"><code>Non_Orig_Ren_Maint_Pct__c</code></p>
<p local-id=3D"995e7c0d070c"><code>Non_Orig_Services_Pct__c</code></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"467710f968e7" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"0a9879b71011">These fields mirror the existing standard perc=
entage fields.</p>
<p local-id=3D"7463dad6946a">They are used only when <code>Deal_Type__c</co=
de> is <code>Fortra Originated</code>.</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h3 local-id=3D"28b42dce0074" id=3D"PartnerPricingV2:BusinessRequirements-E=
xpectedHierarchyPattern">Expected Hierarchy Pattern</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"f86ec442b590">
<li local-id=3D"deb24b131659">
<p local-id=3D"74666d334db7"><strong>Most specific rule:</strong> populate =
<code>Solution_Category__c</code> only.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0b423ee51ee7">
<p local-id=3D"f72fefcf1ffd"><strong>Mid-level rule:</strong> populate <cod=
e>Solution_Group__c</code> only.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c4c0011e32b9">
<p local-id=3D"f70fc6d9a076"><strong>Broad rule:</strong> populate <code>Un=
it__c</code> only.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"da08c8f8cdd9">
<p local-id=3D"ef7452a9ed78"><strong>Fallback rule:</strong> leave all thre=
e hierarchy fields blank.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 local-id=3D"dd62647c65b9" id=3D"PartnerPricingV2:BusinessRequirements-C=
ontextChanges">Context Changes</h2>
<div class=3D"panel" style=3D"background-color: #EBDBC1;border-width: 1px;"=
>
<div class=3D"panelContent" style=3D"background-color: #EBDBC1;">
<p local-id=3D"e205a4632eba">The V2 prehook reads hierarchy values directly=
 from Revenue Cloud context. The quote-pricing context must therefore expos=
e the required quote header and quote-line values.</p>
</div>
</div>
<h3 local-id=3D"cef2c9f7f4ec" id=3D"PartnerPricingV2:BusinessRequirements-R=
equiredContextAttributesandSourceValues">Required Context Attributes and So=
urce Values</h3>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
